From 0287b463c778823dcf043a713c73e0e62e609abf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "HT9045 Machine (V906)" <Claude_RDBC_02@honprec.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 20:40:10 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] HTDESIGNER-23: snap to gridlines -- the WPF designer's grid
 toggle (0.23.0)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The design surface's title bar (#) and right-click menu: 對齊格線（開／關）.
- On: a dotted grid is drawn over the container the selection moves in (else
  the form), aligned to its origin and the zoom; a drag and a resize land the
  moving edges on multiples of the grid (in the element's own px); Alt holds
  it off; with the grid on the sibling snaplines are not used (both at once
  pull against each other); the arrows still move by 1 px, like WPF.
- The size is the setting ht9045Designer.gridSize (default 8, 2..64); on/off
  is shared by every page and kept in the workspace state; the status bar
  shows "格線 8px"; the probe gets it with every init (after a Reload too).

Also: the real VS Code test now records every save its instance makes and
fails on any (NO-SAVES; its own throw-away user settings excepted). The
launcher still compares MD5s -- strictly for the pages and the BCB6 files --
but a port-tree .cpp/.h changed while the test ran and saved nothing is
another session's work: a WARN naming that file's last commit, not a FAIL
(tools/wb_serve.cpp was changed and committed by BRAKE-AXIS 2ea7c90 during
the run).

Tests: probe (grid 8: a drag of +13,+5 -> left 72 top 16, a resize -> 248 x
48, grid drawn 8px 8px; off: not drawn), smoke 84 (on/off told, kept, status
bar), real VS Code 84 (the real probe at 8 px, still after Reload, off again;
NO-SAVES), lib 116, panels -- all pass.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
